<title>UK: TENNIS-DAVIS CUP RESULTS. [CORRECTED 08:30 GMT 13/7]</title>
<headline>TENNIS-DAVIS CUP RESULTS. [CORRECTED 08:30 GMT 13/7]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the second day of</p>
<p>Davis Cup tennis matches on Saturday:</p>
<p>Asia/Oceania zone group one play-off:</p>
<p>In Tashkent: Japan lead Uzbekistan 2-1</p>
<p>Satoshi Iwabuchi/Takao Suzuki (Japan) beat Oleg Ogorodov/Vadim</p>
<p>Kutzenko (Uzbekistan) 6-3 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Euro/African zone group two, second round:</p>
<p>In Bytom, Poland: Poland and Ivory Coast level 1-1</p>
<p>Results (Played Friday, Polish names first):</p>
<p>Michal Chmela lost to Claude N'Goran 4-6 7-5 2-6 7-6 (7-4) 5-7</p>
<p>Bartlomiej Dabrowski beat Jean-Christophe Nadi 7-5 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>Euro-African zone group one play-off:</p>
<p>In Kiev: Britain lead Ukraine 2-1</p>
<p>Tim Henman/Greg Rusedski beat Andrei Medvedev/Dmytro Polyakov</p>
<p>6-1 6-4 7-6 (7-5).</p>
<p>Euro/African zone, group two play-off:</p>
<p>In Tbilisi: Georgia lead Nigeria 3-0</p>
<p>David Kacharava/Vladimir Gabrichidze (Georgia) beat Jean-Louis</p>
<p>Abelekan/Sule Ladipo (Nigeria) 6-7 (10-8) 6-3 6-2 7-5</p>
<p>Euro/African zone group two play-offs:</p>
<p>In Cairo: Egypt lead Lithuania 2-1.</p>
<p>Amr Ghoneim/Hisham Hemeidah (Egypt) beat Rolandas Murashka/Eugenijus Cariovas (Lithuania) 7-6 7-6 4-6 7-6  </p>
<p>Euro/African zone group two, second round</p>
<p>In Nova Gorica: Norway lead Slovenia 2-1</p>
<p>Andrej Krasevec/Marko Por (Slovenia) beat Helge Koll/Christian Ruud (Norway) 6-2 6-3 5-7 1-6 6-2 (corrects to reverse result and make clear Slovenia won today's doubles match)</p>
<p>American Zone, group one</p>
<p>In Buenos Aires: Ecuador lead Argentine 2-1</p>
<p>Results (Ecuadorean names first):</p>
<p>(Matches played on Friday):</p>
<p>Adrian Morejon beat Hernaan Gumy 6-1 6-4 5-7 7-5</p>
<p>Nicolas Lapentti beat Marcelo Charpentier 6-3 6-4 6-3.</p>
<p>(On Saturday):</p>
<p>Lapentti/Giorgio Carneado lost to uis Lobo/Pablo Albano 2-6 1-6 6-7 (4-7)  </p>
<p>Euro/African zone, group two play-off</p>
<p>In Bytom: Poland lead Ivory Coast 2-1</p>
<p>Bartlomiej Dabrowski/Michal Gawlowski beat Claude N'Goran/Lonfo Illou 6-4 7-6 (9-7) 3-6 6-2</p>
</text>
